        },
        {
          "no": 20,
          "code": "Thailand - Boat Transfers",
          "description": "Thailand - Boat Transfers",
          "note": "Pease be informed that regarding the General Luggage Guidelines for \nThailand Boat Transfers:\n\nStandard allowance:\n\nUsually 1 suitcase \u002B 1 carry-on per person is accepted without issue.\nWeight limit:\n\nMost speedboats and shared boats informally expect luggage to be around \n20 kg per person, similar to airline limits. Very heavy bags may be refused \nor require an extra charge.\n\nBoat type matters:\n\nSpeedboats: Limited space \u2192 stricter on size and number of bags\nFerries: More flexible and can handle larger or multiple suitcases\nOversized / special items:\n\nItems such as golf bags, surfboards, diving equipment, baby strollers, or \nwheelchairs must be pre-advised and may incur a supplement or require a \nprivate transfer.\n\nShared vs private transfers:\n\nShared transfers: Stricter luggage control due to space and balance\nPrivate transfers: More flexible, but still subject to boat capacity and safety \nregulations\n \n\nSafety \u0026 weather considerations:\n\nIn rough sea conditions, operators may limit luggage strictly to ensure \npassenger safety.\n\nImportant Note:\n\nFinal acceptance of luggage is always at the discretion of the boat operator, \nand advance notice is strongly recommended if clients are traveling with:\nMultiple suitcases\nHeavy luggage\nSpecial or bulky equipment",
          "dateModified": "2026-01-01T15:28:58",
          "external": true,
          "internal": true,
